{
  "brand": "iolar",
  "template": "spiral-notes",
  "ratio": "3:4",
  "seed": 42,
  "series": "DOCKER IMAGES: LAYERS, CACHE, LEAN BUILDS",
  "date": "29/08/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What an Image Actually Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Image = Layers + Config",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An image is an ordered stack of read-only layers plus a JSON config (env, entrypoint, cmd, workdir, user) and a manifest tying them together. It is addressed by content hash, not by name."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Stack, Bottom Up"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "debian rootfs",
              "+apt packages",
              "+app deps",
              "+app code",
              "writable layer (CoW)"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Layer Mechanics"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Layer = tar of *changes*, not a full snapshot",
            "overlay2 merges the stack into one view",
            "Upper layer shadows lower at the same path",
            "Delete writes `.wh.<name>`; bytes stay forever",
            "Same sha256 = stored once, shared across images"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Where Containers Fit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Container = image layers + 1 thin writable layer",
            "`docker rm` discards only that writable layer",
            "Copy-on-write: 1-byte edit of a 2GB file copies 2GB up"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Which Hash Is Which"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "IDs vs Digests",
          "items": [
            "Image ID = sha256 of the config JSON",
            "RepoDigest = sha256 of the pushed manifest",
            "Tags are mutable: `node:20` today ≠ next week",
            "Pin `node:20@sha256:...` for reproducibility"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Inspect The Layers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker history nginx      # size per layer",
            "docker image inspect nginx \\",
            "  --format '{{json .RootFS.Layers}}'",
            "# [\"sha256:9853...\",\"sha256:5f70...\"]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Deleted ≠ Gone",
          "text": "`rm` in a later layer only writes a whiteout marker. The original bytes still download with every pull."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM python:3.12-slim",
            "COPY --from=build /opt/venv /opt/venv",
            "ENV PATH=/opt/venv/bin:$PATH",
            "CMD [\"python\",\"-m\",\"app\"]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. No Shell State Survives"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN cd /app   # dies with the container",
            "RUN make      # runs in / ✗",
            "WORKDIR /app  # persisted in config",
            "RUN make      # runs in /app ✓"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Chain What Depends"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN apt-get update            # ✗ stale",
            "RUN apt-get install -y curl",
            "RUN apt-get update && \\",
            "    apt-get install -y curl  # ✓"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "One Instruction, One Layer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. One Instruction, One Layer",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Instruction",
            "Layer?",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "FROM",
              "parent",
              "sets base stack"
            ],
            [
              "RUN",
              "yes",
              "fresh container"
            ],
            [
              "COPY",
              "yes",
              "from context"
            ],
            [
              "ADD",
              "yes",
              "auto-untars"
            ],
            [
              "ENV/CMD/WORKDIR",
              "no",
              "config only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Ordering Is Semantic"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`FROM scratch` = empty filesystem, zero layers",
            "Each step runs against the previous result",
            "ENV, LABEL, USER, EXPOSE, ARG: metadata only",
            "Metadata instructions produce zero-byte layers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM scratch      # empty base",
            "COPY hello /hello # the one layer",
            "ENTRYPOINT [\"/hello\"]  # metadata"
          ],
          "note": "metadata instructions add zero bytes"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. COPY vs ADD"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer COPY; ADD untars locals and fetches URLs",
            "`COPY --chown=app:app` skips an extra chmod layer",
            "A later chmod duplicates every file it touches",
            "Layer count is cheap up to a point — overlay2 still caps at 128 lower layers and the daemon rejects images past ~125 with 'max depth exceeded'."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "COPY --chown=app:app src/ /app/",
            "COPY --chmod=0755 run.sh /usr/bin/",
            "# RUN chmod -R /app ✗ recopies all"
          ],
          "note": "a later chmod duplicates every file"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Bytes, Not Steps",
          "text": "Layer count costs nothing meaningful at runtime. Layer content costs everything. Optimize what lands, not how many lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. How The Key Is Built",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Cache key = parent layer digest + this instruction's own key. A miss on one step invalidates every step below it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Key Basis Per Instruction"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Instruction",
            "Cache key",
            "Trap"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "RUN",
              "literal text",
              "never re-resolves"
            ],
            [
              "COPY/ADD",
              "content checksum",
              "mode + owner count"
            ],
            [
              "ARG/ENV",
              "value at use",
              "early ARG, full miss"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cache Keys & Where ARG Belongs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20-alpine",
            "ARG GIT_SHA   # ✗ nukes all below",
            "RUN npm ci    # rebuilt each push",
            "# move ARG down, just before use:",
            "ARG GIT_SHA   # ✓ here: 1 miss",
            "LABEL rev=$GIT_SHA"
          ],
          "note": "declare a changing ARG just before use"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Context, Cache Keys & What Busts Them",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Context Ships First"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Build Context",
          "items": [
            "Classic builder tars and ships the ==whole context== up front",
            "BuildKit (==default since Docker 23==) streams only `COPY`/`ADD` files, cached between builds",
            "3GB dir costs 3GB only if an instruction copies it",
            "`.dockerignore` still earns its keep: cache busts and leaked secrets",
            "Context size and image size are separate costs",
            "BuildKit: DAG, parallel stages, skips unused ones"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "RUN Keys Are Literal Text",
          "items": [
            "Key = the ==command string==, nothing else",
            "Docker never inspects what the command did",
            "Edit a comment inside a RUN and it misses",
            "Same text + old index = **stale** packages"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Edit",
            "What rebuilds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "README.md",
              "`COPY . .` and below"
            ],
            [
              "package.json",
              "`npm ci` and below"
            ],
            [
              "touch, same bytes",
              "nothing — still a hit"
            ],
            [
              "ARG value",
              "its use and below"
            ],
            [
              "base tag moved",
              "only with `--pull`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build --progress=plain .",
            "#  CACHED [2/5] COPY package*.json",
            "#  CACHED [3/5] RUN npm ci",
            "#  [4/5] COPY . .   <- first miss"
          ],
          "note": "everything below the first miss rebuilds"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Bust One Step On Purpose",
          "text": "Put `ARG CACHEBUST` directly above the step, then build with `--build-arg CACHEBUST=$(date +%s)`. Only that step and the ones below it rerun."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ADD https://x.io/t.tgz /tmp/  # ✗",
            "RUN curl -fsSL -o /t.tgz \\",
            "      https://x.io/t.tgz \\",
            " && echo \"$SHA  /t.tgz\" \\",
            "    | sha256sum -c -          # ✓"
          ],
          "note": "ADD never verifies a checksum"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why does a README typo reinstall every dep?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`COPY . .` sits above `RUN npm ci`",
            "New file content = new COPY cache key",
            "So every step below it rebuilds",
            "Fix: copy manifests first, add `.dockerignore`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Ordering Layers So the Cache Holds",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Two Consequences"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`RUN apt-get install -y curl` caches forever — stale software",
            "One source edit rebuilds everything after `COPY . .`",
            "mtime alone does not bust COPY; content does",
            "Golden rule: rarest changes first, source last",
            "Declare a changing ARG just before its use"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Manifest Split"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:20-alpine",
            "WORKDIR /app",
            "COPY package*.json ./  # rare change",
            "RUN npm ci             # stays cached",
            "COPY . .               # hot layer, last"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Same Trick, Any Stack"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Stack",
            "Copy first",
            "Then run"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pip",
              "requirements.txt",
              "pip install"
            ],
            [
              "go",
              "go.mod go.sum",
              "go mod download"
            ],
            [
              "cargo",
              "Cargo.toml/.lock",
              "cargo fetch"
            ],
            [
              "maven",
              "pom.xml",
              "dependency:go-offline"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Where The Miss Starts"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "FROM (hit)",
              "COPY manifest (hit)",
              "RUN npm ci (hit)",
              "COPY . . (MISS)",
              "build + CMD rebuild"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cache Hit ≠ Fresh",
          "text": "`--no-cache` rebuilds everything; `--pull` re-fetches a moved base tag. Schedule both so security patches actually land."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Many FROMs, One File",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each FROM starts a fresh stage with its own stack",
            "Name it: `FROM golang:1.22 AS builder`",
            "Only the final stage's layers ship to the registry",
            "Compilers, headers, source, build caches: discarded"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Go Builder Stage"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM golang:1.22 AS builder",
            "WORKDIR /src",
            "COPY go.mod go.sum ./",
            "RUN go mod download",
            "COPY . ."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cache Mounts, CI Cache & Artifact Handoff",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Persist Across Builds"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "BuildKit + CI",
          "items": [
            "`RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.npm npm ci`",
            "Cache mount ships zero bytes into the image",
            "CI has no local cache — pass `--cache-from` a registry image",
            "`--cache-to type=registry,mode=max` exports intermediates"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Artifact Handoff"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "builder: toolchain + src (900MB)",
              "go build -o /app",
              "COPY --from=builder /app",
              "runtime: distroless (6MB)"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Go Final Stage"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o /app",
            "FROM gcr.io/distroless/static",
            "COPY --from=builder /app /app",
            "ENTRYPOINT [\"/app\"]  # a few MB total"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Node Split + Targets"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "builder: `npm ci && npm run build`",
            "runtime: `npm ci --omit=dev`, copy only `dist/`",
            "Copy from external images: `--from=nginx:alpine`",
            "`--target=builder` builds up to one named stage",
            "BuildKit builds only needed stages, in parallel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Stage Layout"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "base",
              "deps",
              "builder",
              "test (CI only)",
              "runtime"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Files, Not Environment",
          "text": "`COPY --from` carries no ENV, WORKDIR, USER or system packages. A dynamically linked binary in scratch fails 'no such file or directory' — the missing thing is the loader, not your binary."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. What Actually Gets Sent"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "project dir",
              "strip .git .env node_modules",
              "context tar",
              "daemon",
              "COPY . ."
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": ".dockerignore: Filtering the Context",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Why rm Cannot Help"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Earlier Layers Are Immutable",
          "items": [
            "`RUN make && rm -rf /build-deps` shrinks nothing",
            "Deps still sit in the layer that created them",
            "Only a new stage truly drops those bytes",
            "runtime need not depend on the test stage"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Filter Before Upload",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The CLI tars the context and ships it to the daemon before instruction one runs. `.dockerignore` decides what enters that tar."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Where It Lives, How It Parses"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sits at the context root, not beside the Dockerfile",
            "BuildKit also honors `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore`",
            "Go filepath.Match rules, not gitignore rules",
            "`*` does not cross `/`; `**` matches any depth",
            "`#` comments; `!pattern` re-includes; last match wins"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pattern Reference"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Matches"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "node_modules",
              "top level only"
            ],
            [
              "**/node_modules",
              "any depth"
            ],
            [
              "*.log",
              "top-level logs"
            ],
            [
              "!keep.log",
              "re-includes it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Starter File"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "# secrets + junk, one per line",
            ".git",
            "**/node_modules",
            ".env*",
            "*.log"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Allowlist Inversion"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "# deny everything, re-include below",
            "*",
            "!src/",
            "!package.json",
            "!package-lock.json"
          ],
          "note": "only a leading # is a comment"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Three Separate Wins"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Smaller, faster context upload",
            "No cache bust from `.git/` or a stray local log",
            "No `.env`, `*.pem`, `id_rsa`, `.aws/`, `.npmrc` in a layer",
            "Also drop: dist, build, target, __pycache__, .venv, coverage",
            "Verify size: `docker build --progress=plain .`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "node_modules Gotcha",
          "text": "Ignore it and `RUN npm ci` inside the image instead — host-built native modules are the wrong architecture anyway."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Secrets That Must Never Reach a Layer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Layers Are Public",
          "text": "`COPY . .` with no ignore file ships `.git` history and `.env` into a layer. Anyone who pulls can extract them; deleting later does not help."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Secrets Never Reach A Layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ARG TOKEN      # ✗ docker history",
            "RUN --mount=type=secret,id=npm \\",
            "      npm ci   # ✓ never a layer"
          ],
          "note": "the mount lives only for that RUN"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker history` prints every ARG and RUN line",
            "`ENV` also keeps the value in the running container",
            "Pass it at build: `--secret id=npm,src=.npmrc`",
            "Already baked one in? **Rotate** it — `rm` is not enough"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Measuring and Shrinking the Image",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Measure Before Cutting",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker images` for the headline totals",
            "`docker history --no-trunc <img>` for per-layer size",
            "`dive <img>` shows wasted bytes and file diffs",
            "Registry pull cost is what users actually feel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Base Image Dominates"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Base",
            "Size",
            "Use when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "scratch",
              "0MB",
              "static binary"
            ],
            [
              "distroless",
              "~2MB",
              "prod, no shell"
            ],
            [
              "alpine",
              "~7MB",
              "musl is fine"
            ],
            [
              "debian-slim",
              "~75MB",
              "glibc needed"
            ],
            [
              "debian",
              "~120MB",
              "full tooling"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Clean In The Same RUN"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \\",
            "      --no-install-recommends curl \\",
            " && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*  # same RUN"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Per-Tool No-Cache Flags"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Flag"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "apt",
              "--no-install-recommends"
            ],
            [
              "apk",
              "--no-cache"
            ],
            [
              "pip",
              "--no-cache-dir"
            ],
            [
              "npm",
              "ci --omit=dev"
            ],
            [
              "go",
              "clean -modcache"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Slim, Strip, Stage"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`python:3.12-slim` drops docs and dev tooling, keeps glibc",
            "Multi-stage is the biggest lever for compiled languages",
            "`go build -ldflags=\"-s -w\"`, `strip`, CGO disabled",
            "Do not cram one mega-RUN — cache granularity dies",
            "`--platform` mismatch silently pulls an emulated image"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Squash Trade-Off"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "--squash",
          "items": [
            "Merges only the ==newly built== layers into one",
            "Base image layers are **kept** and still shared",
            "Doubles disk use: cache copy + squashed copy",
            "Experimental ==legacy builder== flag; BuildKit ignores it",
            "Multi-stage is the supported way to drop bytes"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN adduser -S -u 10001 app",
            "COPY --chown=10001 dist/ /app/",
            "USER 10001:10001   # numeric = safe"
          ],
          "note": "numeric UID works on distroless too"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "1.1GB to 150MB, Non-Root, Exec Form",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Worked Comparison"
